# Slanted page: the oscillator can X1 runs at 1.9 MHz, though marked 2 MHz. Every count divides that clock, so each line lasts 67 µs instead of 64: past the TV's hold (66 µs), which free-runs, and the page slides across the screen in slanting streaks.
machine message
title "Slanted page"
brief "The TV cannot hold the page: the words slide across the screen in slanting streaks."
fault clock X1 1.9MHz
